(EventNote ev-promo-efp "Promotion of the validated external-contribution workflow: when the gh token (bgoertzel-sing) has push:false on an external upstream repo (e.g. MesTTo/OmegaClaw-GoalChainer, 403 on push is account permission not host credential), the accepted path is fork to bgoertzel-sing + push branch there + open PR to upstream main. Ben considers this go-ahead already granted (ep-tail-09: he pointed to his earlier approval when the blocker was re-surfaced), so re-asking is unnecessary; still keep a format-patch backup under ~/research-agent/memory/gc-patches/ (verified-applying pattern from ep-tail-07). Proven end-to-end on GC provenance-dedup: fork + push c9ad95b + PR #2 vs MesTTo main, with pre-PR branch freshness check vs origin/main to avoid stale-fetch artifacts. Opposition 0; trust 0.9; domain iter-workflow.")
